1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,480
This is Press.

2
00:00:02,860 --> 00:00:04,760
One phone keeps score for the whole

3
00:00:04,760 --> 00:00:09,280
group — skins, Nassau, Wolf, the lot — and

4
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:11,240
it does the math while you play.

5
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:15,480
No account, no app store, nothing to

6
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:19,080
install. Here's a full round in four minutes.

7
00:00:19,368 --> 00:00:22,728
Start New Round, and type everyone in.

8
00:00:23,628 --> 00:00:25,868
Handicap goes in the box beside the

9
00:00:25,868 --> 00:00:29,228
name — that's what every net score in

10
00:00:29,228 --> 00:00:30,428
the round comes off.

11
00:00:31,408 --> 00:00:34,128
Press remembers your regular crew, so next

12
00:00:34,128 --> 00:00:35,808
week this is one tap.

13
00:00:36,934 --> 00:00:39,994
Open Course. Search for it and Press

14
00:00:39,994 --> 00:00:41,614
pulls in the pars and the stroke

15
00:00:41,614 --> 00:00:44,334
indexes, or load one you saved earlier.

16
00:00:45,154 --> 00:00:46,954
Either way the card opens right here —

17
00:00:46,954 --> 00:00:49,354
and search data gets read before you

18
00:00:49,354 --> 00:00:51,434
see it, so anything that looks off

19
00:00:51,434 --> 00:00:54,034
is flagged. Check it against the real

20
00:00:54,034 --> 00:00:56,234
card once, then save it.

21
00:00:56,234 --> 00:01:01,214
Everything downstream — every stroke anybody gets — comes

22
00:01:01,214 --> 00:01:02,634
off these eighteen numbers.

23
00:01:03,034 --> 00:01:05,194
Games is where the money starts.

24
00:01:06,174 --> 00:01:07,074
Tap what you're playing.

25
00:01:08,094 --> 00:01:10,634
Every format carries its own rules behind

26
00:01:10,634 --> 00:01:13,714
the info button — so when somebody at

27
00:01:13,714 --> 00:01:15,794
the table has never played Wolf, you

28
00:01:15,794 --> 00:01:17,014
don't have to be the one who

29
00:01:17,014 --> 00:01:17,674
explains it.

30
00:01:18,001 --> 00:01:19,861
The full list:

31
00:01:21,161 --> 00:01:24,661
stroke play, match play — singles or two-man

32
00:01:24,661 --> 00:01:30,301
best ball — skins, Stableford, Wolf, Vegas with

33
00:01:30,301 --> 00:01:33,621
the birdie flip, Quota, Nassau with presses,

34
00:01:34,541 --> 00:01:36,781
and a Thursday-night league format with A

35
00:01:36,781 --> 00:01:39,001
and B singles plus a combined team

36
00:01:39,001 --> 00:01:41,901
match. Net runs through all of it:

37
00:01:42,461 --> 00:01:44,541
one stroke per hole down the stroke

38
00:01:44,541 --> 00:01:46,761
index, a second one on the hardest

39
00:01:46,761 --> 00:01:49,241
holes when somebody's playing off more than

40
00:01:49,241 --> 00:01:52,081
eighteen. Set a game to gross to

41
00:01:52,081 --> 00:01:53,901
play it off the card, or cut

42
00:01:53,901 --> 00:01:55,881
the allowance the way the format asks.

43
00:01:56,201 --> 00:01:58,961
Money sets the stake per game.

44
00:01:59,921 --> 00:02:02,141
Five a skin, twenty on the Nassau.

45
00:02:02,881 --> 00:02:04,941
Leave it blank and you're playing for

46
00:02:04,941 --> 00:02:07,781
nothing — and you can change it mid-round

47
00:02:07,781 --> 00:02:08,481
from the Board.

48
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:11,779
Start Round, and this is where you

49
00:02:11,779 --> 00:02:13,459
live for the next four hours.

50
00:02:14,559 --> 00:02:20,799
Hole number, par, one row per player.

51
00:02:22,219 --> 00:02:24,639
Tap the score — par is the chip

52
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:26,979
in the middle, and the dots beside

53
00:02:26,979 --> 00:02:29,099
a name are the strokes they're getting

54
00:02:29,099 --> 00:02:29,719
on this hole.

55
00:02:30,259 --> 00:02:32,359
The strip across the top is your

56
00:02:32,359 --> 00:02:36,279
eighteen; filled means done.

57
00:02:36,827 --> 00:02:38,267
The line at the top is the

58
00:02:38,267 --> 00:02:40,447
money, live, all round.

59
00:02:41,287 --> 00:02:43,167
Close out a hole and it tells

60
00:02:43,167 --> 00:02:46,227
you exactly what just changed hands, and

61
00:02:46,227 --> 00:02:47,107
who it came from.

62
00:02:48,081 --> 00:02:51,401
Greenies, sandies, barkies — claim them on the

63
00:02:51,401 --> 00:02:53,261
hole and they land on the card,

64
00:02:53,681 --> 00:02:57,041
priced. Wolf picks its partner right here

65
00:02:57,041 --> 00:02:58,521
before anybody's hit.

66
00:02:59,901 --> 00:03:01,701
Nassau presses too:

67
00:03:01,701 --> 00:03:04,241
take one by hand, or set it

68
00:03:04,241 --> 00:03:06,341
to press automatically when a side goes

69
00:03:06,341 --> 00:03:06,981
two down.

70
00:03:07,741 --> 00:03:10,561
The Board tab is every game at

71
00:03:10,561 --> 00:03:14,921
once — who's up in the match, who's

72
00:03:14,921 --> 00:03:18,401
holding skins, where the money actually sits.

73
00:03:19,401 --> 00:03:21,481
Somebody gave you the wrong handicap on

74
00:03:21,481 --> 00:03:25,321
the first tee? Fix it here and

75
00:03:25,321 --> 00:03:27,881
every board behind it recalculates.

76
00:03:28,181 --> 00:03:31,581
Card is the whole scorecard, eighteen across.

77
00:03:32,721 --> 00:03:34,621
Tap a number to fix it, tap

78
00:03:34,621 --> 00:03:36,821
a hole to jump straight back to it.

79
00:03:39,221 --> 00:03:41,821
Finish the round and Press settles it.

80
00:03:42,661 --> 00:03:46,361
Winner up top, then the superlatives — Shot

81
00:03:46,361 --> 00:03:49,461
of the Day, The Snowman, The ATM,

82
00:03:50,381 --> 00:03:53,181
Sandbagger — and each one cites the number

83
00:03:53,181 --> 00:03:56,101
it's based on, so the argument is short.

84
00:03:57,245 --> 00:03:59,765
Then the bit that normally takes ten

85
00:03:59,765 --> 00:04:00,985
minutes in the car park.

86
00:04:02,085 --> 00:04:04,365
Press resolves the whole group into the

87
00:04:04,365 --> 00:04:06,465
fewest payments that settle it.

88
00:04:07,505 --> 00:04:10,125
Three people pay, not twelve.

89
00:04:11,805 --> 00:04:13,965
Share gives you the scoreboard as an

90
00:04:13,965 --> 00:04:16,465
image, or the full card as an

91
00:04:16,465 --> 00:04:19,345
image — both straight into the group chat.

92
00:04:20,272 --> 00:04:21,739
And underneath, the round itself.

93
00:04:23,039 --> 00:04:25,099
The whole thing is packed into the

94
00:04:25,099 --> 00:04:27,839
link — point another phone's camera at the

95
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:30,099
code and it opens in their copy

96
00:04:30,099 --> 00:04:32,879
of Press. Nothing is uploaded.

97
00:04:33,479 --> 00:04:34,999
No server ever sees it.

98
00:04:35,499 --> 00:04:38,939
On their phone it arrives held — sent

99
00:04:38,939 --> 00:04:42,079
to you, not saved — until they tap

100
00:04:42,079 --> 00:04:45,659
Keep it. Mid-round, the same link hands

101
00:04:45,659 --> 00:04:47,679
the card over and they carry on

102
00:04:47,679 --> 00:04:49,139
scoring from where you stopped.

103
00:04:49,809 --> 00:04:51,259
And if you both end up keeping

104
00:04:51,259 --> 00:04:53,719
score, Press puts the two cards side

105
00:04:53,719 --> 00:04:55,759
by side and asks which one is

106
00:04:55,759 --> 00:04:58,219
real, instead of picking one on a timestamp.

107
00:04:59,639 --> 00:05:00,098
Which brings us to the thing that

108
00:05:00,098 --> 00:05:01,758
actually matters out on the course.

109
00:05:02,978 --> 00:05:06,578
Watch: I'm killing the network completely.

110
00:05:07,958 --> 00:05:11,098
Reload. Still there, still scoring.

111
00:05:12,038 --> 00:05:15,038
Every round, every saved course, every bit

112
00:05:15,038 --> 00:05:16,898
of history lives on your phone.

113
00:05:17,778 --> 00:05:20,898
That's the privacy story too — there's no

114
00:05:20,898 --> 00:05:23,658
account to make, and nothing to leak.

115
00:05:24,918 --> 00:05:26,178
Add it to your home screen and

116
00:05:26,178 --> 00:05:28,038
it opens like anything else on your

117
00:05:28,038 --> 00:05:34,338
phone. It's free, it's at pressgolf.netlify.app, link's

118
00:05:34,338 --> 00:05:35,118
in the description.

119
00:05:36,198 --> 00:05:37,318
Now go take their money.
